      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Harvey Norman installed our solar hot water system quite a few years ago when the government were giving rebates. It wasn't that cheap even with the rebate as the prices were inflated because of that rebate. Once it wasn't being offered the prices dropped dramatically but we weren't to know that at the time. We also weren't to know that it was never properly installed.We did notice there was no difference in our electricity bills but for years just accepted that until recently we really started querying why our bill was always so much higher than other friends we spoke to. We mentioned about having solar hot water and were told to check the solar control near our meter box. What control?? We didn't have this thing, just a circuit breaker makes solar off peak. Really strange as we don't have off peak. We have an electrician coming around to inspect this installation but it appears Harvey Norman never correctly installed our system and one of the reasons we have such high power bills is the booster constantly heating the water, not the solar. Complaint to HN has been met with silence after filling in the form they asked us to.",
